{%- comment -%}
  Warns, before checkout, that part of the cart cannot be collected in store.

  Shopify only says this at the delivery step, as a red "1 item can't be picked
  up" error whose only offered remedy is "Remove item". By then the customer has
  entered an address and picked a method. This says the same thing earlier, in
  calmer language, and offers the remedy Shopify does not: place a second order.

  **Eligibility is `variant-stock-state` returning `own`.** Pickup happens at our
  own locations, and `stock_primary_locations` is already the list of those, so
  no new configuration and no second definition of the same fact. Anything on
  order from a supplier is by definition not on a shelf to collect.

  **Only renders for a mixed cart** — some collectable, some not. That is exactly
  the case that produces Shopify's error. If nothing is collectable Shopify never
  offers pickup at all, and if everything is there is nothing to warn about; in
  both cases this would be noise for a customer who wanted delivery anyway.

  Accepts: nothing — reads `cart` directly.

  Usage:
  {%- render 'cart-pickup-notice' -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign cpn_blocked = 0
  assign cpn_collectable = 0
  assign cpn_updates = ''

  for item in cart.items
    capture cpn_state
      render 'variant-stock-state', variant: item.variant
    endcapture
    assign cpn_state = cpn_state | strip

    if cpn_state == 'own'
      assign cpn_collectable = cpn_collectable | plus: 1
    else
      assign cpn_blocked = cpn_blocked | plus: 1
      comment
        One link clears the lot. /cart/update accepts updates[variant_id]=0 pairs
        as a GET query string, so removing every blocked line is a single href
        with no JS — the per-row links this replaces meant a page load each.
      endcomment
      if cpn_updates != ''
        assign cpn_updates = cpn_updates | append: '&'
      endif
      assign cpn_updates = cpn_updates | append: 'updates[' | append: item.variant_id | append: ']=0'
    endif
  endfor
-%}
{%- if cpn_blocked > 0 and cpn_collectable > 0 -%}
  <div class="cart-pickup-notice">
    <p class="cart-pickup-notice__label">
      {{- 'sections.cart.pickup_notice.label' | t -}}
    </p>
    <ul class="cart-pickup-notice__items list-unstyled" role="list">
      {%- for item in cart.items -%}
        {%- liquid
          capture cpn_row_state
            render 'variant-stock-state', variant: item.variant
          endcapture
          assign cpn_row_state = cpn_row_state | strip
        -%}
        {%- unless cpn_row_state == 'own' -%}
          <li class="cart-pickup-notice__item">
            {{- item.product.title | escape -}}
            {%- unless item.variant.title == 'Default Title' -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                Real separator, not a ::before — generated content is not in the
                text layer, so title and variant ran together as "Racing104".
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <span class="cart-pickup-notice__sep" aria-hidden="true"> — </span>
              <span class="cart-pickup-notice__variant">
                {%- render 'option-value-label', value: item.variant.title -%}
              </span>
            {%- endunless -%}
          </li>
        {%- endunless -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
    <p class="cart-pickup-notice__body">
      {{- 'sections.cart.pickup_notice.body' | t -}}
    </p>
    <a class="cart-pickup-notice__remove" href="{{ routes.cart_update_url }}?{{ cpn_updates }}">
      {{- 'sections.cart.pickup_notice.remove_all' | t -}}
    </a>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
